little background in hockey - never having participated in the World Championships - but built a top team from the ground up for the Seoul Olympics. A third place at the 1987 Champions Trophy signalled their rising power, which was displayed by a crushing defeat of West Germany (4-1) in their first Olympic match. In the final, the home team couldn’t go all the way. The Australians, coached by two-time medallist " [:a {:href "/athletes/17534"} "Brian Glencross"] ", beat them soundly 2-0, leaving the South Koreans crying on the pitch."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button871390", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button871390').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Field Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Corner Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Penalty Stroke Goals"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Long Corner Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-527160"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Australia"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"